  "microscopes": [
    {
      "name": "M2",
      "comment": "Imported from M2's EMU configuration (October 2026), the optics added by hand. Set up with the iXon since July 2026 (the last Evolve stack 2026-07-09, the first iXon one 07-23; the Evolve kept as a version until 07-15). The pixel per lens state, for each camera, was learnt on beads (benchmarks/uipsf/results/lab_beads_pixel.jsonl); the transmitted arm is the brighter half of dual-channel data with two far-red dyes: the right on the iXon (260821), the top on the Evolve (260401), which is turned by 90 degrees against it. EMU's configuration gives the transmitted slider's 685/70 and empty the same value, 10000; empty is put first, so a file reading 10000 is empty and the filter wheel decides: the 561 nm beads of 260917 (wheel 600/60) and the single-mode stacks whose comment says 700/100 read 10000. astigmatism_nm, the start of in situ learning (Noll 6, nm of wavefront, uiPSF v1's sign), from bead models: +62 with the iXon (0.54-0.64 rad at 676 nm, four stacks Aug-Oct 2026, benchmarks/uipsf/results/lab_beads.jsonl and insitu_magnitude.jsonl), -73 with the Evolve, turned by 90 degrees (-0.67 rad, 260622 and 260105).",
      "identify": {
        "Focus-lock-Serial ID": "iBEAM-SMART-785-S-A3-13644"
      },
